# Crocodillian

## Lore

Crocodillians are intelligent, crocodile-like D-bees from an alien dimension
where changing conditions and aggressive predators were driving them to
extinction. The outcast god Sebek rescued several hundred thousand of them,
and out of gratitude and kinship they have served him loyally ever since.
Unlike most evil gods, Sebek genuinely cares for his minions, never spends
their lives foolishly and avenges their deaths. He has settled thousands of
them on Earth, mostly in the rivers of Africa and India, where they live
among ordinary crocodiles (which never molest them) and act as his spies,
helpers and messengers.

They move on all fours, run fast in short bursts and swim like lightning;
they can stand erect but manage only a few paces that way. Their communities
resemble those of their animal cousins - living, hunting and playing in lakes
and rivers - and number from a few dozen to thousands. They are carnivores
that mainly eat animals and fish, and seldom hunt innocent people.

Crocodillians are fairly smart, quick learners and fascinated by technology:
many carry high-tech weapons, gadgets and optics, some take cybernetic
implants, and a fifth are competent computer operators or hackers, though
they design and build nothing. They distrust magic entirely, but every one
of them is psionic.

## GM Notes

Their only formal alliance is with Sebek; they like crocodiles and humans,
dislike the Gods of Darkness (Set and Anubis above all, for Sebek''s
banishment), dislike tautons for giving crocodile-like beings a bad name, find
the Gods of Light meddlesome, and will help those opposing the Four Horsemen.
Alignments run mostly anarchist, unprincipled, miscreant or aberrant. Roll the
psionic type (01-85 master, 86-95 Mind Melter, 96-00 Mind Bleeder) and pick
the matching ability; the dehydration penalties are applied by hand.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'crocodillian');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'crocodillian';

